# Shipped language (process references)

Read project `.ai/kit.yaml` → `process_references` when present.

| Value | Meaning |
|-------|---------|
| `omit` (default if missing) | Do not mention implementation plans, stages/phases, handoff, `AC-*` / `work_ref` as product copy, or `.ai/work/*` paths in product code, comments, public docs, commits, or PR bodies |
| `allow` | Kit does not add this restriction |

Planning may live only under `.ai/` (or gitignored paths).

**User global rules win** when stricter (for example `no-process-language.mdc`). `allow` never weakens a stricter user rule.

Canon: `AGENTS.md` § Shipped language in the kit tree (`kit_root` in `~/.cursor/kit-user-rules.manifest.json`).
